cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EigenOS Quantum Suite - Verifiable Quantum Circuit Compilation submission code"
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite the competition submission it supports.
  The current submission is assembled from three public Apache-2.0 circuits by
  other competitors; NOTICE.md credits every author, licence and URL, and gives
  the SHA-256 of every member of the submitted archive.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Seringian
    given-names: Nicks
    affiliation: EigenOS Quantum Suite
  - name: EigenOS Quantum Suite engineering team
    affiliation: EigenOS Quantum Suite
date-released: 2026-11-02
repository-code: "https://github.com/EigenOS-Quantum/eigenos-vqcc"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Software behind the EigenOS Quantum Suite entry to the Google Quantum AI
  Verifiable Quantum Circuit Compilation competition. The submitted archive holds
  three circuits assembled from published Apache-2.0 work: invsqrt by Ehan
  Mallick (62 qubits, 20.6503x the reference), dqi by Akmal Xodarev on
  SomeJoint's decoder (892 qubits, 64.4371x), and a dfthcsos ANGLE_k family by
  Isabe11aM00re (428 qubits, 10.2676x). Geometric mean 23.9062. We did not
  design these circuits. We assembled them, pinned every one of the 18 members
  with a SHA-256, re-verified all three with the competition's own verifiers on
  the bytes extracted back out of the packed archive, and published the
  generating notebook. The modules under src/gen_invsqrt and src/gen_dfthcsos
  are the generators of our earlier, lower-scoring attempt (public score
  2.53419); they are kept for attribution and do not produce the current
  submission.
keywords:
  - quantum circuits
  - kickmix
  - VQCC
  - verifiable quantum circuit compilation
